+// ---- Safari completion list backdrop (-wex-safarilist), per-process data write ----
+// Safari 27.2 on macOS 26.7.2: CompletionListWindow and AutoFillCompletionWindow return YES from
+// +shouldUseGlassBackdropView, so -[RoundedWindow _createBackdropViewWithContentRect:] creates an NSGlassView, which
+// draws nothing with Liquid Glass (SwiftUI/Solarium) turned off: the list is transparent. Safari is signed with
+// library validation, so no user-space dylib can be inserted.
+//
+// The first version rewrote the two methods in __TEXT through the Lilu page patcher. That modifies the shared file
+// page (UBC) of a compressed file on the sealed App cryptex: when another page of the same 16 KiB verification block
+// is paged in later, APFS hashes the block including the resident patched page, verification fails (EBADMSG) and the
+// faulting thread gets SIGBUS after endless retries (Safari hang + crash, 2026-11-17 09:10).
+//
+// This version leaves the file pages alone. Both senders of shouldUseGlassBackdropView in Safari.framework
+// (0xa8cab, 0x531f89) load the same selector reference, __DATA_CONST 0xc39aa0, send it to a class and test al.
+// After dyld and objc have fixed up the image, the reference is replaced, in the Safari process only, with the
+// uniqued "isProxy" selector taken from Safari's own reference at 0xc21468: +[NSObject isProxy] returns NO.
+// The write goes through a copy-on-write private page of that process (data, not code: no code signing effect).
+// Everything is checked first: process name, LC_UUID of the loaded framework, both selector strings.
